# Local development: leave both unset. Vite's dev server proxies /api and
# /socket.io to http://localhost:5000 (see vite.config.js), so the app
# talks to a single origin with no configuration needed.
#
# Production build (frontend and backend deployed as separate services -
# e.g. this project's documented target of Vercel/Netlify + Render/Railway,
# see ../DEPLOYMENT.md): set both to the backend's deployed URL so the
# built app knows where to send API requests and open its Socket.IO
# connection, since there's no dev-server proxy to do it implicitly.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com
